NSLayoutManager usesDefaultHyphenation, and the two traces that found it.

A 10.15 property was missing, asking for it raised, the raise is caught, and an entire preferences
pane came out half blank with nothing anywhere to say why.

iTerm2 measures every row of its Advanced settings table by laying the row description out and
asking how tall it is. The path is exact:

  -[NSAttributedString(iTerm) heightForWidth:]
  -[iTermAdvancedSettingsViewController tableView:heightOfRow:]
  -[NSTableView noteHeightOfRowsWithIndexesChanged:]

and it sets this switch on the layout manager first. With the selector missing the measurement
threw, every row fell back to a default 17 points, and the pane drew its values and none of its
descriptions.

Stored and answered, which is the whole contract. This framework does not hyphenate either way, so
the value changes no layout here; what matters is that asking does not raise.

AFTER IT: zero unrecognized selectors and zero raises in the run, where there had been one of each,
and the row heights are right, so heightForWidth: is measuring real text now. The value fields are
full width instead of cramped.

NOT FIXED, AND NOT CLAIMED: the description column is still blank. The row heights prove the
description text exists and can be measured, so something else loses it between the model and the
field. That is the next thing.

TWO TRACES KEPT, because aiming at this pane took six runs and three of them were spent on
instruments that could not see it.

  CIDER_TABLE viewForColumn prints, per column and row, what the delegate answers and the string it
  carries AT RETURN TIME, before this table touches it. That is what separates "the application
  never set it" from "we cleared it", and it says the description field comes back EMPTY from the
  delegate while the value column comes back populated.

  CIDER_FRAME now prints the cell view OWN stringValue, not just its subviews'. The loop only asked
  subviews, which covers a wrapper holding a field and misses a cell view that IS the field, so a
  correct 557x17 frame printed with no text beside it and "the column is blank" could not be told
  from "the trace does not ask".

Gates: dts 69 of 69, patch record PASS, roster sweep 7 of 7 CONTENT and all seven unchanged against
the capture baseline, roster input 7 of 7, with iTerm2 looked at.

